    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d505">

                <pb facs="0870" n="738" sameAs="frus:frus1945Berlinv01/pg738"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">860c.01/7–545: Telegram</note>
                <head>No. 505<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in the United Kingdom</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Winant</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the
                        Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Extract]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">secret</hi>
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">London</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1945-07-05T12:00:00+02:00">July 5,
                            1945—noon</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>6749. …</p>
                <p>Same [British] official<anchor n="1" xml:id="d505-f1"/> said that FonOff had
                    concluded yesterday with Polish Govt in London agreement whereby all leases,
                    including lease on Polish Emb property, would be taken over by Brit Govt. Most
                    leases are of short duration but Brit Govt will turn them over to new Polish
                    Govt if it so desires or will continue them on own account.</p>
                <p rendition="#center">. . . . . . .</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Winant</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
